      "writtenOn": "2026-10-31T01:29:15Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "I was unsure how to make them run only on configs that can actually run them.\nBecause techincally they depend on tnvme and on nvme-cli custom commands, so checks like \"if ubuntu-14.04 run, if ubuntu-26.04\" aren\u0027t accurate as this is supposed to also work with with 26.04 in the future.\n\nUpdate:\nThought about it, since it is only temporary, I don\u0027t mind doing the `if 14.04/if 26.04\" check even if it\u0027s not technically accurate and even though it\u0027s ugly, just because it\u0027s temporary until the tests are ported/dropped. Temporary ugly is acceptable.\n\nUpdate 2:\nRemembered that the version in this script refers to which docker image to run the tests from (i.e. which docker image to use to launch **QEMU**, which is still launched from 14.04), so even in the configurations that run the 7.0.2 kernel the version can still be 14.04 (and 5.0.0 can be run from 26.04 docker), so $version can\u0027t tell if the tests should run or not.\nI ended up doing an \"If kernel is on branch master, run tests\". More elegant than by \"If docker image version is ubuntu 14.04\".",
      "parentUuid": "8a585449_29d843ce",
