      "writtenOn": "2026-10-31T01:29:15Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "sourcing env.sh happens before any of the infrastructure runs so doing `make -s kernelrelease` would always be the 5.0.0 (or whatever is in the master branch), so it\u0027s kinda like a chicken and egg problem, this should either be moved to a variable in `configs.json`, or stop using it as a predefined variable and calculate the dist by running `make -s kernelrelease` in the scripts that require that variable.\nSecond option sounds more robust to me.",
      "parentUuid": "78b93ae7_1fe6066b",
      "revId": "4171ce9a61080abf33a123ff1ecc08f999f1ab7c",
