      "writtenOn": "2026-10-31T01:29:15Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Partially answered in the google doc:\n\u003e Variables from `configs.json` are only used from `run-ci.sh`. When running the scripts manually it is intended for the dev to be able to run the scripts using different versions for testing and development, the scripts under `versions/` subfolder furthermore can\u0027t use the `configs.json` values because they are chosen based on the configurations, and not vice versa.\n\nThis file is for compiling the `master` branch, it would be weird if \"Compiling the master branch nvme-cli\" would compile the `3.0-a.5` branch because the `EVSSIM_NVME_CLI_BRANCH` holds that, or vice versa, if \"Compiling the 3.0-a.5 branch nvme-cli\" would compile the `master` branch because the `EVSSIM_NVME_CLI_BRANCH` holds that. These scripts themeselves shouldn\u0027t be affected by EVSSIM_NVME_CLI_BRANCH.\n\nIf anything, the valid issue/suggestion would be that these scripts should be called `versions/nvme-cli/master.sh` and `versions/nvme-cli/3.0-a.5.sh` instead, and then you could call `versions/nvme-cli/EVSSIM_NVME_CLI_BRANCH.sh`, but that creates a different problem where `./compile-guest-tests \u003cubuntu-14.04\u003e/\u003cubuntu-26.04\u003e` no longer tells you which nvme-cli to compile.\n\nUpdate:\nI realize this can be solved by just moving it to a separate `./compile-nvme-cli` step which could then take `master` or `3.0-a.5` as arguments and that solves all three of the problems.\n\n(Leaving this as unresolved in case you dislike this solution)",
      "parentUuid": "067cf890_a3d555d4",
